{
  "info": {
    "name": "Portfolio Manager API",
    "description": "Colección de pruebas de la API de Portfolio Manager.\n\n**Uso:** selecciona el entorno *Portfolio Manager - Local*, completa `adminEmail` y `adminPassword` (los del `.env`) y ejecuta la carpeta **Autenticación** con el *Runner*: las peticiones están ordenadas como un flujo (login → refresh → detección de reutilización → logout) y cada una valida su respuesta. La carpeta **Público** cubre el contenido de la Landing Page (HU001) y no necesita credenciales.\n\nEl refresh token se envía explícitamente en la cabecera `Cookie` (variable `refreshToken`) y el cookie jar se limpia antes de cada petición, para que los resultados no dependan de cookies guardadas. Para que esa limpieza funcione en la app, añade `localhost` en *Cookies → Domains Allowlist*.\n\nFuente de verdad versionada en el repo: `postman/portfolio-manager.postman_collection.json`.\n\nDocumentación interactiva: `{{baseUrl}}/api/docs/swagger-ui.html`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Start every request without stored cookies: the refresh token is sent explicitly.",
          "pm.cookies.jar().clear(pm.variables.replaceIn('{{baseUrl}}'), () => {});"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Keep the latest refresh token issued by the API (login and refresh rotate it).",
          "const refreshCookie = pm.response.headers.all()",
          "  .filter((header) => header.key.toLowerCase() === 'set-cookie')",
          "  .map((header) => header.value)",
          "  .find((value) => value.startsWith('refresh_token='));",
          "if (refreshCookie) {",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', refreshCookie.split(';')[0].substring('refresh_token='.length));",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Autenticación",
      "description": "Flujo completo de HT009 / HU007-HU009. Ejecutar en orden con el Runner.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 · Login con credenciales inválidas → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('Usa el formato de error común', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(401);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Invalid email or password');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.path).to.eql('/api/auth/login');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Wrong#123\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
            "description": "Contraseña incorrecta: el backend no revela si el correo existe."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "02 · Login con datos mal formados → 400",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('Indica los campos inválidos', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(400);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.include('email');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.include('password');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"no-es-un-correo\",\n  \"password\": \"\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "03 · Ruta protegida sin token → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve el error en JSON', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/ping",
            "description": "Cualquier ruta /api/admin/** exige un access token con rol ADMIN."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "04 · Login → 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve un access token Bearer vigente', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.tokenType).to.eql('Bearer');",
                  "  pm.expect(new Date(body.expiresAt).getTime()).to.be.above(Date.now());",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Establece la cookie refresh_token segura', () => {",
                  "  const cookie = pm.response.headers.all().map((h) => h.value).find((v) => v.startsWith('refresh_token='));",
                  "  pm.expect(cookie, 'Set-Cookie refresh_token').to.exist;",
                  "  pm.expect(cookie).to.include('HttpOnly');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookie).to.include('SameSite=Strict');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookie).to.include('Path=/api/auth');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('La respuesta no se cachea', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Cache-Control')).to.eql('no-store'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
            "description": "Guarda `accessToken` y `refreshToken` en las variables de la colección."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "05 · Ruta protegida con token válido → pasa la seguridad",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// No admin endpoints exist yet: any answer other than 401/403 means the token was accepted.",
                  "pm.test('El token es aceptado (ni 401 ni 403)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.not.be.oneOf([401, 403]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/ping",
            "description": "Todavía no hay endpoints de administración: un 404 confirma que el token pasó la seguridad."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "06 · Refresh → 200 (rota el refresh token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.collectionVariables.set('previousRefreshToken', pm.collectionVariables.get('refreshToken'));"]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve un access token nuevo', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Rota el refresh token', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('refreshToken')).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('previousRefreshToken'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Cookie", "value": "refresh_token={{refreshToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "07 · Refresh reutilizando el token anterior → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('Rechaza un refresh token ya rotado', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Cookie", "value": "refresh_token={{previousRefreshToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh",
            "description": "Reutilizar un token rotado se trata como robo: se revocan todas las sesiones del usuario."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "08 · Refresh con el token vigente tras la detección → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('El token vigente también quedó revocado', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Cookie", "value": "refresh_token={{refreshToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "09 · Login (nueva sesión) → 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', pm.response.json().accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "10 · Logout → 204",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('loggedOutAccessToken', pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('loggedOutRefreshToken', pm.collectionVariables.get('refreshToken'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));",
                  "pm.test('Borra la cookie refresh_token', () => {",
                  "  const cookie = pm.response.headers.all().map((h) => h.value).find((v) => v.startsWith('refresh_token='));",
                  "  pm.expect(cookie, 'Set-Cookie refresh_token').to.exist;",
                  "  pm.expect(cookie).to.include('Max-Age=0');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Cookie", "value": "refresh_token={{refreshToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout",
            "description": "Revoca el refresh token (cookie) y el access token (Bearer)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "11 · Refresh tras el logout → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('El refresh token quedó revocado', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Cookie", "value": "refresh_token={{loggedOutRefreshToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "12 · Access token tras el logout → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('El access token quedó revocado (HU009)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{loggedOutAccessToken}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/ping"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Público",
      "description": "Contenido de la Landing Page (HU001, HU002). Accesible sin autenticación.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Perfil público → 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde sin autenticación: 200 con el perfil, o 404 si aún no se configuró', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 404]);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.test('Incluye presentación, contacto y redes sociales', () => {",
                  "    const profile = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(profile.fullName).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(profile.headline).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(profile.about).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(profile.email).to.include('@');",
                  "    pm.expect(profile.socialLinks).to.be.an('array');",
                  "    profile.socialLinks.forEach((link) => {",
                  "      pm.expect(link.platform).to.be.oneOf(['GITHUB', 'LINKEDIN', 'X', 'INSTAGRAM', 'YOUTUBE', 'WEBSITE']);",
                  "      pm.expect(link.url).to.match(/^https?:\\/\\//);",
                  "    });",
                  "  });",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('El 404 usa el formato de error de la API', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(404));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/public/profile"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Tecnologías → 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 200 OK sin autenticación', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Es una lista de tecnologías con categoría válida', () => {",
                  "  const technologies = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(technologies).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  technologies.forEach((tech) => {",
                  "    pm.expect(tech.name).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(tech.category).to.be.oneOf(['BACKEND', 'FRONTEND', 'DATABASE', 'DEVOPS', 'MOBILE', 'TOOLS']);",
                  "  });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/public/technologies"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Proyectos publicados → 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 200 OK sin autenticación', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const projects = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Cada tarjeta trae lo que muestra la Landing Page (HU002)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(projects).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  projects.forEach((project) => {",
                  "    pm.expect(project.slug).to.match(/^[a-z0-9-]+$/);",
                  "    pm.expect(project.name).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(project.shortDescription).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(project.coverImageUrl, 'RN004: imagen principal').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(project.technologies).to.be.an('array');",
                  "    pm.expect(project.featured).to.be.a('boolean');",
                  "  });",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Los destacados van primero', () => {",
                  "  const firstNotFeatured = projects.findIndex((project) => !project.featured);",
                  "  if (firstNotFeatured >= 0) {",
                  "    pm.expect(projects.slice(firstNotFeatured).some((project) => project.featured)).to.be.false;",
                  "  }",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/public/projects",
            "description": "Solo proyectos activos (RN008), destacados primero y luego por orden de aparición."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Perfil público con token inválido → no 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Ignora un Bearer caducado o inválido en las rutas públicas', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 404]);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer expired-or-garbage" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/public/profile"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Documentación",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Especificación OpenAPI → 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 200 OK sin autenticación', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Es una especificación OpenAPI 3 con los endpoints de autenticación', () => {",
                  "  const spec = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(spec.openapi).to.match(/^3\\./);",
                  "  pm.expect(spec.paths).to.have.property('/api/auth/login');",
                  "  pm.expect(spec.paths).to.have.property('/api/public/profile');",
                  "  pm.expect(spec.paths).to.have.property('/api/public/technologies');",
                  "  pm.expect(spec.paths).to.have.property('/api/public/projects');",
                  "  pm.expect(spec.components.securitySchemes).to.have.property('bearerAuth');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/docs/openapi"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "", "description": "Set by the login and refresh requests." },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "", "description": "Latest refresh token, read from Set-Cookie." },
    { "key": "previousRefreshToken", "value": "", "description": "Refresh token before rotation (reuse detection test)." },
    { "key": "loggedOutAccessToken", "value": "", "description": "Access token revoked by the logout request." },
    { "key": "loggedOutRefreshToken", "value": "", "description": "Refresh token revoked by the logout request." }
  ]
}
